      "message": "This might be misleading because unfortunately this is not happening. The panel box always shows: `Failed to load models. Please reload the page.` [1].\n\n\nThe expected handler is reached, but the UI discards its message.\n\n\n- The provider throws `No API token configured...`\n- `ChatModel.getModels()` catches it and correctly stores error.message in `modelsLoadingError`.\n- `PromptBox` converts that string into a boolean:\n```x \u003d\u003e (this.hasModelLoadingError \u003d !!x)``` in [prompt-box.ts (line 100)].\n\n\nIt then displays the same hard-coded fallback for every loading error in [prompt-box.ts (line 164)]\n\nSo this change successfully fixes the endless spinner, but the commit message incorrectly suggests that the host panel `surfaces the reason.` Gerrit stores the reason but does not render it.\n\nA related fix should be done in core in my opinion, until then consider adjusting this commit message.\n\nhttps://imgur.com/a/6PV1Sum",
